-- title:
--   Coefficient identities for Γ₁₅ under Klein's half-turn, part 1
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $\alpha,\beta,s\in K$ satisfy the four relations $\alpha\beta=-s$, $2\alpha^{2}=-5-s$, $2\beta^{2}=s-5$ and $s^{2}=5$. The conclusion is a conjunction of ten polynomial identities in $\alpha$ and $\beta$ with explicit integer coefficients; in each identity the left-hand side is a $\mathbb{Z}$-linear combination of monomials $\alpha^{a}\beta^{b}$ with $a+b=19$ (the first involving the monomials $\beta^{19}$, $\alpha^{5}\beta^{14}$, $\alpha^{10}\beta^{9}$, $\alpha^{15}\beta^{4}$ with coefficients $1,-171,247,57$, the later ones up to sixteen monomials each, with coefficients of size up to about $8\cdot 10^{6}$). Six of the ten right-hand sides are $0$; the remaining four are $-5^{9}\beta$, $57\cdot 5^{9}\alpha$, $-171\cdot 5^{9}\beta$ and $247\cdot 5^{9}\alpha$, occurring as the first, fifth, sixth and tenth conjuncts respectively. Thus each conjunct reduces a homogeneous degree-$19$ expression in $\alpha,\beta$ to an integer multiple of $\alpha$ or of $\beta$, or to zero, modulo the four relations.
--
--   These are the coefficient certificates, for the exponents $u^{0},\dots,u^{9}$, expressing the covariance of the numerator $\Gamma_{15}(u)=u^{15}-171u^{10}+247u^{5}+57$ of the Rubin–Silverberg Möbius datum under Klein's icosahedral half-turn $U=s^{-1}\begin{pmatrix}-\alpha&\beta\\ \beta&\alpha\end{pmatrix}$, the relations being those satisfied by $\alpha=\zeta-\zeta^{4}$, $\beta=\zeta^{2}-\zeta^{3}$, $s=\sqrt5$ for $\zeta$ a primitive fifth root of unity. The statement is a purely algebraic identity over an arbitrary field of characteristic zero, and is used by [`RubinSilverberg.icoU_datumGam`](thm.html#RubinSilverberg.icoU_datumGam), the equivariance of the datum under $U$.
